mac80211 6.18 compat: re-provide positive S1G channel-width flags

Linux 6.18 removed the positive S1G channel-width flags
(IEEE80211_CHAN_1MHZ / 2MHZ / 4MHZ / 8MHZ / 16MHZ) from
enum ieee80211_channel_flags, keeping only the negative
IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_{4,8,16}MHZ variants.

The morse driver only defines these flags itself when building against
mac80211 older than 5.10.11 (see the KERNEL_VERSION(5, 10, 11) guard in
dot11ah/s1g_ieee80211.h) and otherwise assumes the kernel provides them.
That assumption held for 5.10.11..6.17 but breaks on TIP EAP115, which
uses OpenWrt backports 6.18.7. The result is:

  dot11ah/s1g_channels_rules.c:29:33: error: 'IEEE80211_CHAN_1MHZ' undeclared
  ... (also 2MHZ / 4MHZ / 8MHZ)

Re-provide the original definitions for mac80211 >= 6.18. These bits are
only consumed internally on the driver's own struct ieee80211_channel
.flags entries to derive the operating bandwidth (op_bw_mhz / op_ch_bw in
dot11ah/s1g_channels.c); they are not handed back to the mac80211
regulatory core. The bit values match the driver's own <5.10.11
definitions so the internal set/read logic stays consistent.

NOTE: build-level compatibility fix for Linux 6.18, matching the scope of
Morse Micro's own 6.18 workaround. Runtime behaviour on 6.18 is not yet
validated by Morse (officially supported up to 6.12).

Signed-off-by: EdgeCore <dev@edge-core.com>

--- a/dot11ah/s1g_ieee80211.h
+++ b/dot11ah/s1g_ieee80211.h
@@ -220,7 +220,25 @@ static inline bool ieee80211_next_tbtt_present(__le16 fc)
 }
 
 #endif
 
+#if KERNEL_VERSION(6, 18, 0) <= MAC80211_VERSION_CODE
+/*
+ * Linux 6.18 removed the positive S1G channel-width flags
+ * (IEEE80211_CHAN_1/2/4/8/16MHZ); the morse driver only defined them
+ * itself for mac80211 < 5.10.11 and relied on the kernel otherwise.
+ * Re-provide them for 6.18+ so the driver's private S1G channel tables
+ * keep building. Driver-internal use only (bandwidth derivation); not
+ * handed back to mac80211's regulatory core.
+ */
+enum morse_dot11ah_channel_flags_6_18 {
+	IEEE80211_CHAN_1MHZ	= BIT(14),
+	IEEE80211_CHAN_2MHZ	= BIT(15),
+	IEEE80211_CHAN_4MHZ	= BIT(16),
+	IEEE80211_CHAN_8MHZ	= BIT(17),
+	IEEE80211_CHAN_16MHZ	= BIT(18),
+};
+#endif
+
 #if KERNEL_VERSION(4, 12, 0) > MAC80211_VERSION_CODE
 struct ieee80211_bss_max_idle_period_ie {
 	__le16 max_idle_period;
